1
00:00:04,668 --> 00:00:13,898
Quote, invoice, get paid — Billing ▸ Quotes & Invoices — The self-pay path: price it up front, invoice it, take the money.

2
00:00:19,212 --> 00:00:28,082
Billing ▸ Quotes & Invoices is the self-pay side — programmes, cosmetic work, anything no insurer is covering.

3
00:00:28,082 --> 00:00:36,079
The tabs are the lifecycle: Quotes, then Invoices, then Payments, with coupons and reminders alongside.

4
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:47,985
Quote first. A price agreed before the work starts is the cheapest way to avoid an argument after it.

5
00:00:47,985 --> 00:00:52,929
Pick the patient the quote is for.

6
00:00:52,929 --> 00:01:01,187
Pull the line straight from the service catalogue and the price comes with it — no typing numbers from memory.

7
00:01:01,187 --> 00:01:07,541
Everything is itemised, so the patient can see what each part costs.

8
00:01:07,541 --> 00:01:19,022
Give it a valid-until date. A quote without an expiry is a price you have promised forever.

9
00:01:19,022 --> 00:01:29,143
Say what is included. Most billing disputes are really scope disputes.

10
00:01:29,143 --> 00:01:34,935
Saved and ready to send. Until the patient accepts, nobody is committed.

11
00:01:34,935 --> 00:01:42,184
Once they accept, convert it to an invoice — same lines, same price, now a demand for payment.

12
00:01:42,184 --> 00:01:48,943
The invoice is what gets paid, and the payment closes it. Accounting picks it up from there.

13
00:01:50,471 --> 00:02:06,201
What you just did

14
00:02:07,361 --> 00:02:16,361
